      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_998ed2e0",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: gallows; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man being hanged by masked individuals, with overlaid text including phrases like \"traitors,\" \"pure evil,\" \"nobody escapes this. nobody,\" \"bring back the gallows!\", and \"she never thought she would lose. until she did.\" The visual of execution combined with the text suggests a call for violent retribution against a specific group or individual, framed as a moral or political victory. The phrase \"bring back the gallows\" is a direct reference to historical execution methods, implying a desire for extreme punishment. The meme uses the imagery of state-sanctioned violence to incite hatred and support for punitive measures against a target, which aligns with hateful intent. The text \"she never thought she would lose. until she did\" implies a narrative of betrayal and downfall, further fueling resentment and a desire for retribution. The overall intent is to incite hatred and support for violent retribution against a specific group or individual, using the imagery of execution to justify extreme punishment.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
